 ## Overview
-NeRDi is a single-view synthesis method that leverages general image priors from a pre-trained 2D diffusion model to optimize a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) [S2]. It solves the problem of novel view synthesis from a single input image by minimizing the diffusion loss of rendered arbitrary views under input view constraints [S2]. Unlike traditional NeRF which relies on multi-view consistency or explicit geometric supervision, NeRDi uses a pre-trained diffusion model as a regularizer, supplemented by semantic and geometric guidance to ensure multi-view consistency and 3D structural validity [S2].
+NeRDi is a single-view synthesis method that leverages a pre-trained 2D image diffusion model to provide general image priors, enabling high-quality novel view synthesis from a single input image [S1, S2]. Unlike traditional NeRF variants that rely on multi-view consistency or explicit geometric supervision alone, NeRDi minimizes the diffusion loss of rendered arbitrary views under input view constraints [S2]. It distinguishes itself by introducing semantic guidance via language embeddings and a geometric loss based on estimated depth maps to regularize the underlying 3D structure [S1].
 
